\title{drawn: Design-Based Sampling with Known Inclusion Probabilities}
\description{
Draws probability samples from data frames under an explicit, reusable sampling design: simple random, stratified, systematic, cluster, multi-stage, weighted (including probability-proportional-to-size), reservoir, bootstrap, temporal and spatial. A design is a value that can be stored, printed and reused, and that knows its own first- and second-order inclusion probabilities, so a drawn sample carries the weights needed for Horvitz-Thompson estimation and 'ht_total()' returns a population total with a standard error and confidence interval. Designs whose inclusion probabilities have no closed form report that rather than supplying an approximation, and can be estimated by simulation instead.
